* bench_rtd: platinum RTD, Callendar-Van Dusen equation with the IEC 60751 A and B coefficients (valid 0 to 850 C).
* R(T) = R0 * (1 + A*T + B*T^2), A = 3.9083e-3 /C, B = -5.775e-7 /C^2 (IEC 60751:2008). The C term (below 0 C) is not modelled.
* T is the temperature in C, carried on a stimulus node (stim) so that it can be driven by a source.
.subckt bench_rtd a b params: R0=100 T=0
VSTIM stim 0 DC {T}
RSTIM stim 0 1G
B1 a b I={V(a,b)/(R0*(1+3.9083e-3*V(stim)-5.775e-7*V(stim)*V(stim)))}
.ends bench_rtd
